{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Household Survey Coverage",
  "subtitle": "Coverage by village and enumerator, and submission trends",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total submissions",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Unique enumerators",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"enumerator_name\") AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Submissions per village",
    "sql": "SELECT \"village\" AS village, COUNT(*) AS submissions FROM \"household_survey\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 20",
    "x": "village",
    "y": [
     "submissions"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Submissions per enumerator",
    "sql": "SELECT \"enumerator_name\" AS enumerator, COUNT(*) AS submissions FROM \"household_survey\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10",
    "x": "enumerator",
    "y": [
     "submissions"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Submissions over time",
    "sql": "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', CAST(\"_submission_time\" AS TIMESTAMP)) AS month, COUNT(*) AS submissions FROM \"household_survey\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "month",
    "y": [
     "submissions"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard shows that {{p1}} households were surveyed, with {{p2}} enumerators covering the work. The bar chart in {{p3}} highlights that the village with the highest coverage is {{p3.village}} with {{p3.submissions}} submissions, while the lowest is {{p3.village}} with {{p3.submissions}}. In {{p4}}, enumerator {{p4.enumerator}} led the effort with {{p4.submissions}} submissions, followed by {{p4.enumerator}} with {{p4.submissions}}. The line chart in {{p5}} illustrates a steady increase in submissions, peaking in {{p5.month}} with {{p5.submissions}} entries, indicating growing survey activity over time."
 },
